diff --git a/DOCS/man/vf.rst b/DOCS/man/vf.rst
index a1f036a..720cc59 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/vf.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/vf.rst
@@ -771,6 +771,26 @@ Available mpv-only filters are:
         Enable NVIDIA RTX Video HDR processing. This only converts SDR to HDR,
         so it is ignored when the source is already HDR.
 
+``nvidia-vfg``
+    NVIDIA Video Frame Generation using the Video Effects SDK. It synthesizes
+    intermediate frames between adjacent video frames and supports multipliers
+    from 2 to 8. The default is 2x with the medium model.
+
+    Requires a compatible NVIDIA GPU and the NVIDIA VFX SDK Core plus the Video
+    Frame Generation feature and model. NVIDIA distributes those components
+    separately through NGC; mpv does not include them. If the SDK runtime or
+    feature cannot be loaded, this filter passes video through unchanged.
+
+    The filter converts frames through pinned host memory, which may limit
+    real-time performance at high resolutions. It supports 8-bit SDR and
+    packed 10-bit HDR input; output frames retain the source color metadata.
+
+    ``mode=<low|medium|high>``
+        Select the NVIDIA VFG model (default: medium).
+
+    ``multiplier=<2..8>``
+        Select the output frame-rate multiplier (default: 2).
+
 ``amf_frc``
     AMD Frame Rate Conversion filter. Requires AMD hardware and drivers
     supporting AMF FRC.
